  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till HIPS - startegisk utvecklingsplan f&#xf6;r   2015/2016</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the Heritage Institute for Policy Studies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SIDA support is aimed to strengthen the institute as an independent Somali-owned and Somali-managed think tank. The core support has been crucial in ensuring continued operation of HIPS as an independent policy institute. Hence, the support has strengthened HIPS institutional capacity, increased its research output, expanded its policy engagement as well as enabled it to augment and diversify its funding streams.
HIPS five-year strategic plan objectives&#xa0;are:Strategic objective 1: To develop programs and conduct research in the priority thematic areas of peace, justice and good governance.Strategic objective 2: To foster inclusive public dialogues that will influence policy, increase transparency and accountability and inform HIPS research agenda.Strategic objective 3: To ensure sufficient staff in both numbers and capacity to deliver organizational objectives.Strategic objective 4: To fully computerize the core and support functions of HIPS activities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">The Heritage Institute for Policy Studies (HIPS) har ans&#xf6;kt om st&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n Sida p&#xe5; totalt MSEK 4 f&#xf6;r genomf&#xf6;randet av sin strategiska plan  &quot;HIPS strategic development plan 2015-2016&quot; i Somalia under perioden 1 oktober 2015 till 31 December 2016. 

Insatsen syftar dels till att st&#xe4;rka institutet i sin roll som en nationell think tank och dess kapacitet att kunna p&#xe5;verka policybeslut genom att bland annat producera &quot;policy briefs&quot; baserat p&#xe5; dess tematiska forksknings- och p&#xe5;verkansprogram. Detta st&#xf6;d inbegriper d&#xe4;rf&#xf6;r i) st&#xe4;rkandet av den institutionella strukturen, ii) st&#xe4;rkt kapacitet f&#xf6;r resursmobilisering, iii) &#xf6;kad personalkapacitet, iv) st&#xe4;rkt finansiell administrativ kapacitet. Insatsen syftar ocks&#xe5; till att st&#xf6;dja implementeringen av HIPS strategiska utvecklingsplan 2015 som inkluderar tematiska forsknings- och p&#xe5;verkansprogram . HIPS kommer &#xe4;ven att genomf&#xf6;ra en trendanalys av Sveriges st&#xf6;d till Somalia.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Heritage Institute for Policy Studies (HIPS) has applied to Sida for funding of 4 million SEK to carry out the &apos;&apos;HIPS strategic development plan 2015-2016&apos;&apos; in Somalia during the period 1 October 2015 to 31 December 2016. 

The intervention aims at strengthening HIPS which is a national policy institute to be able to play their role more effectively as a think tank influencing policy decisions on Somalia by producing policy briefs from their thematic research programs and outreach and impact programs. Therefore the support aims at i) institutional structure strengthening, ii) increased capacity for resource mobilization, iii) increased human resource capacity, iv) increased financial administration capacity. The intervention also aims at supporting the implementation of the HIPS strategic development plan 2015 which includes thematic research programs and outreach and impact programs. The Research, Analysis and Development Evaluations (RAADE), with is a unit within HIPS will also conduct a trend analysis of Swedish support in Somalia.</narrative>
  </description>
